1
00:00:02,100 --> 00:00:04,510
The top button of the drawing bar sets the cursor.

2
00:00:04,610 --> 00:00:07,470
Cross, dot or arrow, an eraser for drawings, or zoom in on an area.

3
00:00:07,570 --> 00:00:16,590
Demonstration draws a trail that fades, handy when you show the chart to someone.

4
00:00:16,690 --> 00:00:23,120
This button adds icons and emoji to mark the chart.

5
00:00:23,220 --> 00:00:26,140
This button opens the side panel.

6
00:00:26,240 --> 00:00:30,870
Data Window shows the values of the candle under the cursor.

7
00:00:30,970 --> 00:00:35,410
Objects lists the drawings on this chart.

8
00:00:35,510 --> 00:00:38,420
Close the panel with its X. Each chart remembers if its panel is open.

9
00:00:38,520 --> 00:00:45,120
This button turns trading from the chart on and off: your trade lines hide or show.

10
00:00:45,220 --> 00:00:50,970
The menu at the top of the bar can clear all drawings.

